/**
 * F4 screen 10 (Enterprise Licensing) test fixtures - VERBATIM rig
 * captures from the live open rig (:5100) on 2026-10-16, taken in two
 * passes from Temp/opencode/cap10 (scratch, never staged):
 *
 * 1. read captures of the demo deployment: the license list, the active
 *    license's detail (one imported event), its signed JSON file, the
 *    /api/v1/meta catalog and the /api/v1/overview aggregates.
 * 2. a real write-lifecycle run for a scratch SUBSCRIPTION license
 *    (minted with the rig's own bind-mounted signing key through the
 *    product's LicenseGenerator - the vendor tool path): import -> 201,
 *    duplicate import -> the honest 409 refusal, offline validate -> the
 *    server's verdict (captured twice: for the scratch envelope and for
 *    the demo license's own envelope), revoke with reason -> 200,
 *    restore -> 200, revoke again -> the terminal state. Every response
 *    body is what the server answered, refusals included.
 *
 * Rig hygiene: the scratch license (31ED5F43) is REVOKED (terminal) and
 * the demo license (62070B33) was never touched; both JWT fixtures are
 * the server's raw `text/plain` file answers (base64url
 * header.payload.signature), captured verbatim - the active license's
 * own token and the revoked scratch license's own token.
 *
 * The list fixture carries two rows - the active demo enterprise license
 * and the revoked scratch subscription license - so status chips, tier
 * variety and the revoked row's restore affordance are all real data.
 */

